  <h1>Mathematical Foundations of Neuroscience &amp; Neural Co-Processors</h1>
  <p class="lead">Biological nervous systems are not a computing metaphor — they are literal physical instances of partially observed, mutually adapting, boundary-reshaping systems. Here we build the mathematical foundations of neuroscience and closed-loop brain–computer interfaces from first principles: dynamical descent and intrinsic manifolds, exact Sum-of-Squares stability and barrier certificates over \(\mathbb{Q}\), proof-gated neural interfaces, cognitive inhibition, and synthetic synesthesia.</p>

